X:1
T:Blest Be The Tie That Binds
T:BOYLSTON
C:Music: Lowell Mason, 1832 · Words: John Fawcett, 1782
S:Open Hymnal Project ABC (openhymnal.org; marked public domain), melody line with every stanza as printed there; their source: "The Psaltry" 1845 by Lowell Mason Page 151. In The Psaltry, the Tenor carries the melody. It is moved to the Soprano. The Soprano is then lowered one octave an. Melody cross-checked against the hymnary.org score (hymnary.org/tune/boylston_mason): 100% of pitches and 100% of note lengths agree.
M:3/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=90
K:C
