w: Blest be the tie that binds Our hearts in Christ- ian love;
w: Be- fore our Fa- ther's throne We pour our ar- dent prayers;
w: We share each o- ther's woes, Our mu- tual bur- dens bear;
w: When we a- sun- der part, It gives us in- ward pain;
w: This glor- ious hope re- vives Our cou- rage by the way;
w: From sor- row, toil and pain, And sin, we shall be free,
G | E/ F/ G G | A/ B/ c B | c/ A/ G G | G2 |]
w: The fel- low- ship of kin- dred minds Is like to that a- bove.
w: Our fears, our hopes, our aims are one Our com- forts and our cares.
w: And of- ten for each o- ther flows The sym- pa- thi- zing tear.
w: But we shall still be joined in heart, And hope to meet a- gain.
w: While each in ex- pec- ta- tion lives, And longs to see the day.
w: And per- fect love and friend- ship reign Through all e- ter- ni- ty.
